{"archetypes":[{"name":"scope-anchor-flow","focus_area":"risk-integration","weight":1,"rationale":"The diff threads a new staged scope anchor through many plan-review components where miswiring could silently reintroduce brainstorm or stale scope.","prompt_body":"Trace how the staged scope anchor is created and passed through scout, reviewer panel, voters, revise, and MainAgent fallback. Look for any path that still uses brainstorm-merged context, stale implement-session feature text, or an unstaged outside path as binding scope evidence. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"scope-marker","focus_area":"correctness","weight":1,"rationale":"The new leading [SCOPE-REDUCTION] marker detector affects collect, dedup, aggregation, and tally behavior and has narrow false-positive rules.","prompt_body":"Review the scope-reduction marker detection and all call sites that rely on it. Check whether severity-prefix stripping, fenced-code and inline-code exclusions, heading or Concern parsing, and non-leading tag rejection match the plan across shell and Python snippets. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"plan-aggregation","focus_area":"correctness","weight":1,"rationale":"Plan-mode aggregation now excludes tagged findings from LLM merge, appends them back, validates preservation, and renumbers headings.","prompt_body":"Inspect the plan-mode aggregation and dedup-to-ballot path for marker preservation, reviewer coverage, fallback behavior, and sequential heading renumbering. Pay special attention to mixed tagged and untagged findings, duplicate FINDING headings, and whether validation uses the correct source file after splitting tagged blocks. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"env-handoff","focus_area":"risk-integration","weight":1,"rationale":"SCOPE_ANCHOR_FILE is persisted through multiple result-env layers where allowlist or sanitization gaps could break MainAgent fallback.","prompt_body":"Follow SCOPE_ANCHOR_FILE through inner loop output, run-step3-review parsing, phase-driver result env writing, SKILL handoff parsing, and MainAgent fallback use. Verify CR/LF handling, allowlists, early exits, and later-wins semantics are consistent with existing result-env contracts. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"prompt-boundary","focus_area":"security","weight":1,"rationale":"The change inlines issue scope text into reviewer, voter, revise, and fallback prompts and depends on untrusted-data framing to avoid prompt injection.","prompt_body":"Review every prompt surface that includes scope-anchor or feature text for clear untrusted-evidence framing. Check that user-controlled issue text is not presented as instructions, that only requirement and scope facts are requested, and that default prompt behavior remains unchanged when the new flags are omitted. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"pr-metrics","focus_area":"risk-integration","weight":1,"rationale":"The diff adds PR line-count reporting outside the main scope, so integration failures could affect final reports without plan-review tests catching them.","prompt_body":"Examine compute-pr-line-counts, render-run-summary, and write-final-report integration for non-fatal behavior, gh api pagination assumptions, repo-unavailable handling, numeric validation, and quiet-stream compatibility. Check whether failures or missing PR data degrade to N/A or skipped status without aborting final report publication. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."}]}
